  "caveat": "Value to RMP's system at day-ahead prices, per MW of fleet. Beat 6 assumes the fleet does not move prices; this curve estimates how value per MW falls if it does. The slope of PACE price on PACE net load is confounded by gas prices, imports and the wider EDAM footprint that sets the price, so it is an estimate with an interval, not a forecast. 500 MW is the MOU ceiling, not installed capacity.",
  "model": "The price in each Mountain hour moves by slope x fleet MW x the fleet's net injection per MW: discharge lowers it, charging raises it. Negative slopes are clamped to zero and flagged; an hour whose interval spans zero is marked inconclusive. The off-peak rule and the timetable are fixed schedules, repriced. The hourly DP (1 MW, 2 MWh, as fix.py) re-plans seeing its own price impact. The band puts every hour at its interval's upper slope (low) and lower slope (high).",
